# ALL.prelude -- the text corpus_suite_harness.py prefixes to the first line of every entry of this package (SCRIP c0286d9d9).
# CEO-1712 (the ceo on hq_prolog's two asks, 2026-10-14): this package's refs are cut from swipl, so its programs run in SCRIP's SWI
# dialect, selected the way the swi_tests shim selects it -- the COMPILE-TIME marker the SWI arms read (a use_module directive:
# prolog_lower.c pl_dialect_marker), not the run-time flag alone -- and with swipl's double_quotes string. It is the program's own
# declaration of the oracle that answers it, not a compatibility switch.
# hq_icon 2026-10-25 (the cto's ARCH-PROLOG-DIALECTS.md sec 6 (1), the package contract, CEO-1964/1958): the two lines above this note -- the
# SWI marker and swipl's double_quotes string, written for swipl's refs -- are gone; XSB 5.0.0 cuts the refs, so the prelude carries ONE XSB
# marker, :- compiler_options([]). (below the operators, which must parse first), and SCRIP reads every entry in its XSB dialect:
# double_quotes codes as XSB's default, '$dialect' xsb, an XSB marker outranking the use_module line each vendored file begins with.
# CEO-1958 (the ceo 2026-10-24, on the cfo's ask under CEO-1927): XSB 5.0.0 cuts this package's refs, so the prelude declares the three operators
# XSB's own reader holds (syslib/file_op.P: import fy 1050, export fx 1100, from xfx 1040) that the programs' module directives are written in --
# 611 :- import ... from ... lines and 9 :- export ... lines; SCRIP's import/1 and export/1 already answer the directive.
:- op(1050, fy, import).
:- op(1100, fx, export).
:- op(1040, xfx, from).
# hq_icon 2026-10-24 (CEO-1926, the same reading of CEO-1958): XSB's reader also holds index fy 1100 (syslib/file_op.P), the prefix form of XSB's
# indexing directive -- 9 :- index Name/Arity-Arg lines in 6 files, ai_tests/can_mono.P's two among them, which every ai_tests program imports
# from; SCRIP's index/1 answers the directive (an indexing hint, no answer changes).
:- op(1100, fy, index).
# hq_icon 2026-10-28 (CEO-1926): the rest of the operators XSB's reader holds (syslib/file_op.P '_$op1', XSB 5.0.0) that SCRIP's reader lacks, in XSB's own priorities and types, so a program written
# in them parses as XSB reads it: the prefix forms do_all (fx and xfy 1150) and if_none (xfy 1150) of XSB's do_all/1,2, the tabling and threading declarations (use_variant_tabling, use_subsumptive_tabling,
# use_incremental_tabling, use_incremental_dynamic, use_opaque_tabling, thread_shared, thread_private, edb), the file and module declarations (ti, ti_off, mode, mode_on_success, annotation,
# document_export, parallel, local, foreign_pred, private_foreign_pred, compile_command, attribute at 1100, document_import 1050), the renaming import's infix as (xfx 1045: :- import P from M as Q.),
# tnot (fy 900) and the infix >< (yfx 500). Measured neutral on every entry that passed before; foreign_tests_test_importas needs `as`.
:- op(1150, xfy, do_all).
:- op(1150, fx, do_all).
:- op(1150, xfy, if_none).
:- op(1100, fx, use_variant_tabling).
:- op(1100, fx, use_subsumptive_tabling).
:- op(1100, fx, use_incremental_tabling).
:- op(1100, fx, use_incremental_dynamic).
:- op(1100, fx, use_opaque_tabling).
:- op(1100, fx, thread_shared).
:- op(1100, fx, thread_private).
:- op(1100, fx, edb).
:- op(1100, fy, ti).
:- op(1100, fy, ti_off).
:- op(1100, fx, mode).
:- op(1100, fx, mode_on_success).
:- op(1100, fx, annotation).
:- op(1100, fx, document_export).
:- op(1100, fx, parallel).
:- op(1100, fx, local).
:- op(1100, fx, foreign_pred).
:- op(1100, fx, private_foreign_pred).
:- op(1100, fx, compile_command).
:- op(1100, fx, attribute).
:- op(1050, fy, document_import).
:- op(1045, xfx, as).
:- op(900, fy, tnot).
:- op(500, yfx, ><).
:- compiler_options([]).
